It is necessaray that an EntityType has one and only one Name
It is necessary that an Attribute has one and only one Name
It is necessaray that an EntityType has one and only one FullyQualifiedName
It is necessary that an Attribute has one and only one FullyQualifiedName
It is necessary that each FullyQualifiedName uniquely references a single object
It is necessary that a Name is a string value
It is necessary that a Label is a string value
It is obligatory that a Name must conform to a chosen NamingConvention
It is necessary that an Attribute's Name is unique within the contextual scope of its parent Entity
It is necessary that an Entity's Name is unique within the contextual scope of its parent Namespace
It is obligatory that a FullyQualifiedName must conform to the FQN specific NamingConvention
It is necessary that an EntityType contains zero or more Attributes
It is necessary that an Attribute is part of one and only one EntityType
It is encouraged that an EntityType has at least one Label
It is encouraged that an Attribute has at least one Label
It is encouraged that a Relationship has a Name
It is necessary that a Relationship has zero or one Names.
It is necessary that a Relationship contains one and only one targetRole
It is necessary that a Relationship contains one and only one sourceRole
It is necessary that a targetRole is a Role
It is necessary that a sourceRole is a Role
It is necessary that a Role is part of a Relationship and only one Relationship
It is necessary that a Role is associated with an EntityType and only one EntityType
It is obligatory that an EntityType has a Definition
It is obligatory that an Attribute has a Definition
It is obligatory that a Definition be written using Intensional form
